    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (where YY is the last two digits of the registration date's year, e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` field mapped to a `membership_number` column, plus its getter/setter, alongside the existing derived fields.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (controller) \u2014 in `addOwner`, after the customer code and registration date are assigned, I set the membership number via a new `membershipNumber(...)` helper that formats `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`. It's fixed at creation time, consistent with how `customerCode`/`namesakeCount` are handled.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema so it's on the generated `OwnerDto` and returned by the API (MapStruct auto-maps it by name).\n\n4. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `membership_number` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat` \u2014 which creates an owner and asserts `customerCode + \"-M\" + yy` equals the returned `membershipNumber` \u2014 passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
